ition characterized by an increased metabolic rate, which is often observed in critically ill patients. This heightened metabolic state can also occur in individuals with liver disease, resulting in muscle loss and various other complications.", "CALORIMETRY:Calorimetry is a method used to measure energy expenditure, which is crucial for determining the nutritional needs of patients. This technique is particularly recommended for assessing metabolic rates in individuals with liver disease. In clinical settings, calorimetry is frequently employed to evaluate the metabolic needs of patients, providing valuable insights into their energy requirements. Overall, calorimetry serves as an important tool in understanding and managing the metabolic health of patients.", "LIPOLYSIS:", "PACIENTE CIRRÓTICO:El paciente cirrótico es una persona que padece cirrosis, una enfermedad hepática crónica que afecta su estado nutricional y requiere valoración nutricional.", "EDEMAS:EDEMAS refers to swellings that occur due to excess fluid being trapped in the body's tissues. This condition can be particularly concerning for patients with kidney issues, as it may indicate underlying health problems. Additionally, edemas can complicate nutritional assessments in patients with cirrhosis, as the accumulation of fluid in the tissues can affect overall health and nutritional status.", "RESTRICCIONES DIETÉTICAS:Las restricciones dietéticas son limitaciones en la ingesta de ciertos alimentos que pueden ser necesarias para el manejo del paciente cirrótico.", "MUSCLE STRENGTH:Muscle strength is a vital component in evaluating the nutritional status of patients with cirrhosis and plays a significant role in the assessment of sarcopenia. It is commonly measured using handgrip dynamometry, which is a standard method for quantifying muscle strength. Additionally, muscle strength can be assessed through various tests, including handgrip strength and knee extension. Overall, muscle strength serves as an important physical attribute that reflects an individual's health and functional capacity.", "BIOELECTRICAL IMPEDANCE ANALYSIS:Bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) is a method used to estimate body composition, including fat and lean mass, which is relevant in nutritional assessments.", "ROYAL FREE HOSPITAL NUTRITIONAL PRIORITIZING TOOL:The Royal Free Hospital Nutritional Prioritizing Tool (RFH-NPT) is a global scheme for assessing nutritional risk in patients with cirrhosis.", "PACIENTES CIRRÓTICOS:PACIENTES CIRRÓTICOS refers to individuals suffering from cirrhosis, a serious liver condition that often leads to nutritional deficiencies. These patients require specific dietary assessments and nutritional guidelines to effectively manage their condition. Proper nutrition is crucial for cirrhotic patients to support their health and mitigate the complications associated with their illness.", "ROYAL FREE HOSPITAL:The Royal Free Hospital is a healthcare institution that utilizes the Nutritional Prioritizing Tool (RFH-NPT) for assessing malnutrition risks in patients.", "EHC:EHC refers to patients with chronic liver disease, particularly those experiencing sarcopenia, which is a significant concern in nutritional management."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}